Completing the squares gives the standard equation of a <circle>:
$$
\left(x+\frac12\right)^2+(y+1)^2=\frac94.
$$
Its centre is therefore
$$
\boxed{\left(-\frac12,-1\right).}
$$

= b
{parent=9}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

In the completed-square equation, the right side is the squared radius of the <circle>. Taking its positive square root gives
$$
\boxed{r=\frac32.}
$$

